WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.435
-It's so nice to see you
in person.

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:04.937
Thank you so much
for doing our show

00:00:04.937 --> 00:00:06.939
during Zoom, the shows --

00:00:06.939 --> 00:00:08.941
you know, you're a friend
of the show.

00:00:08.941 --> 00:00:11.111
I appreciate it. Thank you.
-Thanks for having me back.

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:12.611
Hi, everyone!
-Come on.

00:00:12.611 --> 00:00:14.947
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Ahh!

00:00:14.947 --> 00:00:16.782
-Well, I want to talk
about your stand-up special.

00:00:16.782 --> 00:00:18.952
Premiers tonight, HBO Max.

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:20.620
That's gigantic.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:21.821
That's fantastic.
-Dream come true.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:23.323
Dream come true. I'm so pumped.

00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:24.824
-But you also have
a book of essays,

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:28.027
called "Please Don't Sit on My
Bed in Your Outside Clothes."

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:29.028
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:30.863
Explain the title to me.

00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:32.699
-[ Laughs ] Do you get it?

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:34.033
Questlove gets it.

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.869
So, you know, my parents
are very neat people.

00:00:36.869 --> 00:00:38.370
They like a clean home.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.372
And they're like,
"The outside world is triflin'.

00:00:40.372 --> 00:00:42.208
Don't bring that in here."

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:44.210
So they would tell my brother
and I, just like,

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.045
change clothes --
put on your inside clothes.

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:47.547
Put on your pajamas or whatever.

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:50.716
And then that stuck with me, and
so then when I went to college,

00:00:50.716 --> 00:00:52.218
went to Pratt Institute,

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:55.888
I wouldn't let anyone sit
on my bed in my dorm,

00:00:55.888 --> 00:00:57.223
'cause I'm like, "You were
on the New York subway,

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.558
so you can't sit on there."

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.559
And then so many people
were like...

00:01:00.559 --> 00:01:03.062
That was the one thing
people remembered about me,

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:05.364
so I was like, "Oh, my
personality was trash

00:01:05.364 --> 00:01:06.866
in college."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:08.201
So... [ Laughs ]

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:10.003
-That's so...
-Yeah, it's horrible.

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:11.204
-I love that.
-Yeah.

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:12.872
-And do you still kind of
feel that way, or no?

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.207
-Yeah. Yes.

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:17.209
No, just please, just bring
an overnight bag.

00:01:17.209 --> 00:01:18.711
Just bring a change --

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.479
Please don't sit on my stuff!
-I love that that's what they

00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:24.149
remember about you, like of all
the funny things you're doing.

00:01:24.149 --> 00:01:25.652
No, what's what you remember,
that I said...?

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:27.820
-Yeah.
-I love that.

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:29.488
I want to talk about
the stand-up special

00:01:29.488 --> 00:01:33.993
because you shot this
in the middle of the pandemic,

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:36.329
at the botanical gardens?
-Yeah, in Brooklyn.

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:38.330
-In Brooklyn, which is you,
which I love.

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:39.665
-Yeah.
-What was it like?

00:01:39.665 --> 00:01:41.000
-It was very exciting.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.668
I was so nervous
'cause I was like,

00:01:42.668 --> 00:01:45.404
I just hope we can get this off,
you know, with the delta.

00:01:45.404 --> 00:01:47.573
The delta variant was like,
"Hey, Boo!"

00:01:47.573 --> 00:01:49.242
And I was like...

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:51.243
I was like, "This is my moment!
Please!"

00:01:51.243 --> 00:01:53.079
And we got through it.
-"Hey, Boo."

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:54.914
-Yeah. "Hey, Boo! I'm back!"

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:56.749
-[ Laughs ] No!
-I'm like, "No one invited you."

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:58.250
-Look at this spot.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:01.588
-Look at those Peloton legs,
you guys.

00:02:01.588 --> 00:02:04.090
[ Cheers and applause ]
Look at it!

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:06.425
Aah! Look at it!

00:02:06.425 --> 00:02:09.762
-Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:12.932
But I love that you did it

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:14.433
and you go, "Yeah,
we're doing this safely

00:02:14.433 --> 00:02:16.603
and we're putting this out there
'cause we need funny."

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:18.104
-Yes!
-We need content.

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:19.839
-We gotta just, like, relax

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:21.841
and laugh and not be
stressed out anymore.

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:24.344
So, I hope that people feel that
way when they watch the hour.

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:25.845
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:28.347
Here's Phoebe Robinson
in "Sorry, Harriet Tubman."

00:02:28.347 --> 00:02:29.681
Take a look at this.

00:02:29.681 --> 00:02:31.016
-Now, don't get me wrong.

00:02:31.016 --> 00:02:32.518
I love my boyfriend. I do.

00:02:32.518 --> 00:02:35.354
He's my soul mate,
my best friend.

00:02:35.354 --> 00:02:37.356
But during quarantine,

00:02:37.356 --> 00:02:39.025
he was giving me major

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:42.028
"Do you have a moment to talk
about the environment?"

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:44.364
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:47.033
You know those guys
on the street with vests,

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.535
holding clipboards,
just getting in your way?

00:02:49.535 --> 00:02:51.403
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.403 --> 00:02:53.572
Asking you questions.

00:02:53.572 --> 00:02:54.941
That was my boyfriend.

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:58.578
He was just trapping me
all over the apartment, okay?

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:01.581
He's like, "Are you hungry?
Want to order out?"

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:03.583
"Do you want to watch a movie
or play checkers?"

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:05.084
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:07.586
"Hey, I'm just checking in.
I want to see how your day is."

00:03:07.586 --> 00:03:12.925
And I was like, "Man, you have
an uncut, livestream feed

00:03:12.925 --> 00:03:14.927
of how my day is going!"

00:03:14.927 --> 00:03:16.095
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:17.763
-You tell me! Exactly right.

00:03:17.763 --> 00:03:19.598
Phoebe Robinson, everybody!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:19.598 --> 00:03:22.602
"Sorry, Harriet Tubman"
is streaming right now

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:23.669
on HBO Max!

00:03:23.669 --> 00:03:25.738
It's out! Congratulations!
-Whoo!

